  "source": [
    {
      "kind": "client",
      "evidence": "Global.Text 74754 'Hooligan Bullies!' (title), 74755 (card), objective 74757; icon 310."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reference",
      "evidence": "Starter: reference Npcs.json Id 4162 drawn at [-1924.36, -52.16, 275.29] (npc_spawns_extra.json spawn_guid 100000004162, FreeRealms-Legacy FabledRealms.lua). Region The Wilds, place The Wilds."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reference",
      "evidence": "BJX fork Resources/Battles.json Id 58 ('Hooligan Bullies! (the live random encounter: hooligan bullies)'): scene sg_random_encounter_01, entry, exit, 3 waves, 10 spawns ({'Hooligan': 7, 'Hooligan Archer': 2, 'Hooligan Scrapper': 1})."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Every spot inside the scene is the fork's generated layout, not an original one. Zone number 1239 is the fork's; ours must be assigned and the scene sg_random_encounter_01 has not been loaded by our server yet (the eleven shipped battles all use sg_random_encounter_clearing). Triggers: at-start spawns are actors, later waves follow the one before (the fork's 1.5 s delay is dropped). Knockouts and score are the design's defaults; coins and XP are the shipped battles' values, not the fork's 15 coins / 100 stars."
    },
    {
      "kind": "wiki",
      "evidence": "The quest step and the wiki put 'Hooligan Bullies!' in this fight; the fork's layout had 'hooligan' there. (R) 'Hooligan Bullies!' takes those spots (wiki over the fork's roster)."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Not proven in the client: this scene needs one native load, and the starter or door of `entry` is drawn by the entrances work, not by this file. Each kind's rank here decides its health and hit at the fight's tier."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) rc-0136 (2026-11-11): model 203 human_m_hooligan_brawler_01.agr (the Hooligan's body); the fight's waves field this kind, and 1913 sg_spawner_human_01.adr is the battle starter's tent prop (Legacy NPC 4162), not a fighter."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) rc-0136 (2026-11-11): this row is the battle's starter, the prop 2014 drew it as (the Snarler's den: video 5-IM2pBh2yY frames 01048 and 01080, red name, crossed swords, Press X; capture p12 t=546051.7 model 1938). The fight's own kind carries the body its waves fight with."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) rc-0137 prize wheel (2026-11-12): 'Hooligan Bullies!' has no wheel of its own on the wiki; the wiki's item pages put its prize wheel with 'Mudshell' (Ninja's Shadow Blade of Soul Power; Wizard's Ornate Wand of Chaos; Warrior’s Warlord Axe of Command; Medic's Shockrod of Antibodies), so it spins that wheel, from fandom 'Mudshell' (revision 30403), one per combat job, and 10 coins. Conflict: its own row says difficulty 1 (the fork's), while 'Mudshell' is difficulty 5; the fight keeps its difficulty. The same pages also name Chugawump, Chugawump!. Brawler: the wiki's 'Bare-Knuckle Brawler Shoulder Pads' is 'Bare-Knuckle Brawler Shoulderpads' in our record dungeons/mudshell.json; Brawler: the wiki's 'Brawer's Atlas Hammer of Rage' is 'Brawler's Atlas Hammer of Rage' in our record dungeons/mudshell.json."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) rc-0137 (owner: the hooligans 'say no lines' and 'don't all come at the player'): each bully, archer and the Scrapper says one of its own lines when it engages and now and then while it fights (L1189, owner 2026-11-12: 'the hooligans saying they could bench you'): Global.Text 37156-37170, the brawler-initiation block of the client locale; bullies 37156-37160/37164, the Scrapper 37162/37163/37165/37166 ('I can bench ten of you!'), archers 37167-37170. The chase is the engine's battle rule (no notice radius in a paced fight, as the captured Frostfang wave wolves); the melee default's 40 m had left the far wave points idle (w1 spawns 35 to 41 m from the arrival)."
    }
  ]
}
